  "query_preview": "..\n\nAn upper-level ridge over the Central US is interacting with an \nupper-level low over NORCAL and an upper-level trough over \nManitoba/Ontario, producing SW flow aloft over Montana. Minor \nperturbations moving throughout the flow may create localized \nareas of instability, potentially producing isolated showers \nthrough early this morning near the North Dakota border. \nPrimarily trace precipitation is anticipated, although there is \npotential for a hundreth or two in the SE Yellowstone Valley.\n\nThe Canadian trough and ridge over the Central US will exit \neastward while the low over NORCAL digs south and becomes cut-off\nover southern Nevada by Tuesday morning. The low's associated \ntrough will encompass the majority of the Intermountain West, \nsomewhat stiffling potential trough development over Canada and \nenabling predominantly zonal flow over Montana through Wednesday \nmorning. Subsequent warm, dry, and gusty conditions Tuesday will \nbe cause for fire weather concerns.\n\nAn upper-level low in northern Manitoba will begin to dig south \nWednesday, warping zonal flow into an upper-level trough that will\nreach as far south as South Dakota. An associated front will \nproduce Wednesday night temperatures cool enough to possibly \nresult in frost on river bottoms. Individuals with outside plants \nthat are still alive may wish to bring them inside beforehand.\n\nThe cold will not be long-lived; a developing high-pressure ridge\nover the West Coast will build over NE Montana by Thursday.\n\nAgreement between models begins to break down at this point, but \nan oncoming upper-level trough is anticipated to dig over Montana \nsometime between Friday night and Saturday afternoon. Confidence \nin timing is low, but enjoy the fair weather in the meanwhile.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Low to moderate confidence in chances for showers through this\n  morning.\n\n- Low to moderate confidence in FireWx Tuesday afternoon. \n\n- Moderate confidence in partial frost Thursday morning.\n\n\nDON",
